script = ExtResource("2_nv63m")
letter_id = 250
description = "[font_size=32](1/3)    Purple,

I visited the craziest place last week. Have you ever been to Arroyo Springs? I was looking for the bottle we left in 1799. It should’ve aged perfectly. I figured I’d ask the bartender, considering the saloon was built right where we expected. They called it, “The Old Hare” saloon. I always wanted to use one of those spittoons. 

I sidled up to the bar “Give me your most expensive whisky.” I made sure to put the proper [i]Twang[/i] on it, you know?

“Lookin for this?”

I turned around, in the corner there was a short man sitting, he barely had a face beneath the brim of his hat and his massive mustache. On the table there was a bottle of Mad Igna’s burning whisky, probably aged about a hundred years. 

Now this was frustrating. I asked him how much.

“Just a game.” 

I told him “alright, one game.”

“Name’s Slim,” he said, fanning out the cards.

He dealt out hands. What he wasn’t aware of was the fact that I had a state of the art 3029 probability scanner on hand. No bumpkin from no-where Arizona was going to beat that. Before I even picked up the cards I knew it was going to be a pair of queens, a winning hand in this game. Without having to worry all I had to do was pretend to be a little bit folded. I might even make it look like I'd think about folding. But no, they’d know I was bluffing, what I had to do was [i]pretend[/i] to bluff. Slim looked at my grin, “Hey kid, house always wins,” he said. "
letter_format = ExtResource("1_6tn4d")
